Package: reyos-browser
Version: REPLACE_VERSION
Section: web
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Rey Paulino
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, python3-pip, kdialog, libnotify-bin, libnspr4, libnss3, libxcb-cursor0, libatk1.0-0t64, libatk-bridge2.0-0t64, libcups2t64, libdrm2, libgbm1, libxcomposite1, libxdamage1, libxfixes3, libxrandr2, libxkbcommon0, libasound2t64, libpango-1.0-0, libcairo2, libxss1, libxtst6, fonts-liberation, libxkbfile1, libpulse0, libpcsclite1
Description: Reyva -- private-by-default web browser from ReyOS
 A native Qt/PySide6 web browser with tracking protection, Shields,
 password manager integration, and "install as app" support.
 .
 This package builds its own Python virtual environment at install
 time (see postinst) instead of shipping a pre-built one. A prior
 hand-built venv ended up with its PySide6 install incomplete (CLI
 helper scripts present, the actual package missing from
 site-packages -- most likely an install cut short by low disk space),
 and the app silently failed to launch (ModuleNotFoundError: PySide6)
 with no visible error, since desktop launchers show no terminal.
 Building fresh from requirements.txt at install time, from a tracked
 source instead of an ad hoc staging directory, removes that failure
 mode.
